      {
        "id": 129041,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-24T01:17:31.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Reckless\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/48/2467_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Reckless:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Like an inside joke that the established forum members get.&nbsp; I'm not saying it's a bad thing.&nbsp; It's just something that will need to be explained to new members, just like the acronyms or initialisms that we've used for certain decks, characters, and card sets.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>There really isn't anything there to \"get\". And really, the forum still makes sense if you for some reason can't work out that occasionally someone (usually me) expresses comedy exasperation at a particular person. It doesn't need \"explaining\". It isn't the same as jargon or uncommon game-specific terms.</p>\n<p>A post full of abbreviations/obscure names is difficult or impossible for a person who doesn't have sufficient game knowledge to understand. I don't like that and think we should minimise it where we can, especially as we get more and more characters and cards and more new members.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:03:54.576Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
